  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (177 tests, 0 failed).\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release` follow your spec, with every time check going through the store's `clock`.\n- `confirm` also returns the SKU, which the API uses for its response.\n- `removeItem` now checks against available stock, so it can't remove reserved units.\n- An expired reservation stays in the map. Confirming it keeps giving `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` instead of turning into `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`. The cost is that expired entries are never cleaned up.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`.\n- `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the statuses you listed.\n- Any `POST /reservations` error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` returns 400, with the error message as the body.\n\n**Tests**\nI added 6 store tests and 5 API tests. They cover the expiry boundary, where a reservation expires exactly at creation time plus `ttlMs`. They also cover the confirm errors, idempotent release, and `removeItem` against reserved stock.\n\nI didn't add validation for `ttlMs`. A missing or non-numeric value gives a reservation that never expires, because the comparison with `NaN` is always false.",
